<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions 4.85 billion rupees' bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions 4.85 billion rupees' bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned six-month short-term federal bonds worth 4.85 billion rupees on Saturday.</p>
<p>The bank received bids worth 11,914.82 million rupees out of which bids worth 4,854.82 million were accepted at a weighted average yield of 16.41519 percent per annum, a bank statement said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.62 rupees) -- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
